      "text": "First, let's denote the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0\\) by \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\). By Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships for the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0\\):\n\n1. \\(a + b + c = -3\\),\n2. \\(ab + bc + ca = 4\\),\n3. \\(abc = 11\\).\n\nNext, we need to find the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0\\), which are given by \\(a+b\\), \\(b+c\\), and \\(c+a\\). We will find the value of \\(t\\), the constant term of this polynomial.\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the roots \\(a+b\\), \\(b+c\\), and \\(c+a\\):\n\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a + b + c) = 2(-3) = -6.\n\\]\n\nThus, the coefficient \\(r\\) of \\(x^2\\) is \\(-6\\). Next, we calculate the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) + (b+c)(c+a) + (c+a)(a+b).\n\\]\n\nExpanding each term, we get:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) = ab + ac + b^2 + bc,\n\\]\n\\[\n(b+c)(c+a) = bc + ba + c^2 + ca,\n\\]\n\\[\n(c+a)(a+b) = ca + cb + a^2 + ab.\n\\]\n\nAdding these together, we have:\n\n\\[\nab + ac + b^2 + bc + bc + ba + c^2 + ca + a^2 + ab = 2(ab + bc + ca) + (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\n\\]\n\nWe know from Vieta's formulas that \\(ab + bc + ca = 4\\). Next, we need to find \\(a^2 + b^2 + c^2\\). Using the identity \\(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 = (a+b+c)^2 - 2(ab+bc+ca)\\), we substitute the known values:\n\n\\[\na^2 + b^2 + c^2 = (-3)^2 - 2 \\cdot 4 = 9 - 8 = 1.\n\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time is:\n\n\\[\n2(ab + bc + ca) + (a^2 + b^2 + c^2) = 2 \\cdot 4 + 1 = 8 + 1 = 9.\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate the product of the roots:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca) - abc = (-3)(4) - 11 = -12 - 11 = -23.\n\\]\n\nThus, the constant term \\(t\\) in the polynomial \\(x^3 - 6x^2 + 9x - 23 = 0\\) is \\(-23\\). Therefore, the value of \\(t\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-23}.\n\\]",
