      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given the polynomial equation \\(x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0\\) with roots \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\), we know from Vieta's formulas that:\n\\[a + b + c = -3,\\]\n\\[ab + bc + ca = 4,\\]\n\\[abc = 11.\\]\n\nWe need to find the sum of the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0\\) whose roots are \\(a+b\\), \\(b+c\\), and \\(c+a\\). By Vieta's formulas for this new polynomial, the sum of the roots is given by:\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a+b+c).\n\\]\nSince \\(a + b + c = -3\\), we have:\n\\[\n2(a+b+c) = 2(-3) = -6.\n\\]\nTherefore, the sum of the roots of the new polynomial is \\(-6\\), which means:\n\\[\nt = -6.\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\(t\\) is \\(\\boxed{-6}\\).",
