      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given that \\( a, b, \\) and \\( c \\) are the roots of the polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\), we can use Vieta's formulas to find the relationships between the roots and the coefficients of the polynomial. From Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\\[\na + b + c = -3,\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4,\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11.\n\\]\nThe problem states that the roots of the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) are \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\). We need to find the value of \\( t \\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the roots of the new polynomial:\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a + b + c) = 2(-3) = -6.\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient \\( r \\) is:\n\\[\nr = -6.\n\\]\nNext, we calculate the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) + (b+c)(c+a) + (c+a)(a+b).\n\\]\nExpanding each term, we get:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) = ab + ac + b^2 + bc,\n\\]\n\\[\n(b+c)(c+a) = bc + ba + c^2 + ca = bc + ac + c^2 + ba,\n\\]\n\\[\n(c+a)(a+b) = ca + cb + a^2 + ab = cb + ab + a^2 + ca.\n\\]\nAdding these together, we have:\n\\[\n(ab + ac + b^2 + bc) + (bc + ac + c^2 + ba) + (cb + ab + a^2 + ca) = 2(ab + bc + ca) + (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\n\\]\nWe know \\( ab + bc + ca = 4 \\), so:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 4 + (a^2 + b^2 + c^2) = 8 + (a^2 + b^2 + c^2).\n\\]\nTo find \\( a^2 + b^2 + c^2 \\), we use the identity:\n\\[\na^2 + b^2 + c^2 = (a+b+c)^2 - 2(ab+bc+ca) = (-3)^2 - 2 \\cdot 4 = 9 - 8 = 1.\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\n8 + 1 = 9.\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient \\( s \\) is:\n\\[\ns = 9.\n\\]\nFinally, we calculate the product of the roots of the new polynomial:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (ab + ac + bc + ba)(a+b+c) - abc = (2(ab + bc + ca))(a+b+c) - abc = 2 \\cdot 4 \\cdot (-3) - 11 = -24 - 11 = -35.\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient \\( t \\) is:\n\\[\nt = -35.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\( t \\) is \\(\\boxed{-35}\\).",
